# ── Vibes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Runtime state. Producer output lands in .vibes/received/ and is NEVER
# committed: `vibes accept` is the only thing that writes a committed baseline.
#
# The `.vibes/*` form is required, NOT `.vibes/`. A directory-form ignore makes
# git skip the directory entirely, so a `!` negation inside it can never take
# effect and policy.lock.json would stay invisible. (Verified 2026-08-21.)
.vibes/*
!.vibes/policy.lock.json

# Snapshot baselines ARE committed — they are the product. Re-include them
# against the repo-wide bare-extension rules above (*.log, *.tmp, *.bak,
# *.backup), which otherwise reach INTO a snapshot dir and silently hide a
# produced file, making the report show zero changes forever.
!**/vibes/snapshots/**
# Ingest artifacts are per-run and carry timestamps; never snapshot-compare them.
**/vibes/artifacts/
